---
title: Download the Final Light Quick Start | Questadon
permalink: /final-light-quickstart/index.html
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
# The one place the filenames live. Re-cut a PDF under a new name and these
# are the only lines to change - the public URL never moves. Sizes are read
# from the files at build time.
rulesUrl: /downloads/final-light-quick-start-rules.pdf
gmUrl: /downloads/final-light-quick-start-gm.pdf
---
{# Download page for the Final Light Quick Start.

   This page exists to make the downloads countable. A direct link to a PDF
   runs no JavaScript, so GA4 can never see it; landing here first means each
   button can fire an event as it hands over its file.

   It offers two buttons rather than starting a download on load: browsers
   block a page from downloading several files on its own. Each button opens
   its PDF in a new tab - the browser's own viewer, which on a phone is where
   readers can save it or send it to Books - and leaves this page in place
   for the other file.

   Because this is a real page, UTM tags on the URL work too:
   /final-light-quickstart?utm_source=kickstarter picks up channel attribution
   in GA4 for free. #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>{{ title }}</title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  {# Not a page we want in search results - it exists to hand over files. #}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
  <link rel="preload" href="/assets/fonts/general-sans-variable.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg">
  {# Same theme bootstrap as layout.njk, so this page opens in the visitor's
     chosen palette instead of flashing the dark default. #}
  <script>
    (function() {
      var theme = localStorage.getItem('theme');
      if (!theme) {
        theme = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light';
      }
      document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', theme);
    })();
  </script>
  <style>
    @font-face {
      font-family: 'General Sans';
      src: url('/assets/fonts/general-sans-variable.woff2') format('woff2'),
           url('/assets/fonts/general-sans-variable.woff') format('woff');
      font-weight: 200 700;
      font-display: swap;
    }

    /* Palette lifted from styles.css so this standalone page stays on brand. */
    :root {
      --color-bg:    #08100a;
      --color-text:  #f0f0df;
      --color-primary: #ED1E79;
      --color-secondary: #E6FF7C;
    }

    :root[data-theme="light"] {
      --color-bg:    #f6feef;
      --color-text:  #05220c;
      --color-primary: #ED1E79;
      --color-secondary: #266201;
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      padding: 2rem 1.25rem;
      background: var(--color-bg);
      color: var(--color-text);
      font-family: 'General Sans', system-ui, sans-serif;
      text-align: center;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .gate { max-width: 30rem; width: 100%; }

    .gate__logo {
      width: clamp(160px, 40vw, 260px);
      height: auto;
      margin: 0 auto 2rem;
      display: block;
    }

    .gate__heading {
      font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 2rem);
      font-weight: 600;
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    }

    .gate__note {
      margin: 0 0 2rem;
      opacity: 0.85;
    }

    .gate__files {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.875rem;
      max-width: 22rem;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .gate__file {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      padding: 0.9rem 1.25rem;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      background: var(--color-primary);
      color: #fff;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 1.0625rem;
    }

    .gate__file:hover,
    .gate__file:focus-visible { filter: brightness(1.1); }

    .gate__file:focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--color-secondary);
      outline-offset: 3px;
    }

    .gate__size {
      font-weight: 400;
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      opacity: 0.9;
    }

    :root[data-theme="light"] .gate__file { background: #A20041; }

    .gate__back {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      color: var(--color-text);
      opacity: 0.7;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="gate">
    <img class="gate__logo" src="/assets/final-light-logo-web.png" alt="Final Light" width="400" height="200">
    <h1 class="gate__heading">Download the Quick Start</h1>
    <p class="gate__note">
      <em>Local Anaesthetic</em>, the learn-to-play Quick Start for Final Light,
      comes in two PDFs. Players need the rules; the GM needs both.
    </p>
    <div class="gate__files">
      <a class="gate__file" href="{{ rulesUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-file="{{ rulesUrl }}">
        Quick Start Rules
        <span class="gate__size">PDF, {{ rulesUrl | fileSize }}</span>
      </a>
      <a class="gate__file" href="{{ gmUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-file="{{ gmUrl }}">
        Quick Start GM Book
        <span class="gate__size">PDF, {{ gmUrl | fileSize }}</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <a class="gate__back" href="/projects/final-light-ttrpg/">&larr; Back to Final Light</a>
  </div>

  {% set gaBeacon = true %}
  {% include "analytics.njk" %}
  <script>
    {# Custom event name rather than GA4's built-in `file_download`, which
       Enhanced Measurement also fires on its own for these clicks. Keeping our
       own name means the count is exactly "times this page handed over a
       file", split by file_name, with nothing else mixed in. #}
    document.querySelectorAll('.gate__file').forEach(function(link) {
      link.addEventListener('click', function() {
        gtag('event', 'quickstart_download', {
          file_name: link.dataset.file.split('/').pop()
        });
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
